WEBVTT

00:00:11.220 --> 00:00:16.266
Musashino of the good old days
is preserved here, in this town of

00:00:16.266 --> 00:00:18.268
Higashi-Koganei.

00:00:18.268 --> 00:00:18.644
In the peaceful residential district

00:00:18.644 --> 00:00:20.145
"Metropolitan Koganei Park"
In the peaceful residential district

00:00:20.145 --> 00:00:22.022
"Metropolitan Koganei Park"
is where the building stands...

00:00:22.898 --> 00:00:24.149
Mouse House.

00:00:24.149 --> 00:00:27.361
Young girls who aim to become
tomorrow's top idols

00:00:27.361 --> 00:00:30.614
obey strict codes imposed on them day and night,

00:00:30.614 --> 00:00:34.368
and work diligently together here,
in this harsh yet warm dream--

00:00:48.382 --> 00:00:50.592
I'm the first one today!

00:00:52.010 --> 00:00:52.970
Wha--?!

00:00:52.970 --> 00:00:54.388
Could it be...?

00:00:54.388 --> 00:00:56.348
Not again?!

00:00:57.099 --> 00:00:59.351
"Meiou"

00:00:59.351 --> 00:01:01.228
"Meiou"
Don't pass out in the bathroom!

00:01:01.228 --> 00:01:05.065
"Meiou"
Code #1: The morning bathroom
is first come, first serve!

00:01:10.112 --> 00:01:13.907
Only use the minimum amount of toilet paper.

00:01:13.907 --> 00:01:16.618
Air freshener spray time is
limited to less than three seconds.

00:01:17.578 --> 00:01:19.913
Sorry for the wait!

00:01:19.913 --> 00:01:21.331
Okay.

00:01:21.331 --> 00:01:25.002
Nina, you've got 28 seconds deducted
from your bathroom time tomorrow.

00:01:25.002 --> 00:01:27.754
Can't you be a little more lenient for a girl?!

00:01:27.754 --> 00:01:31.341
Code #2: Keep your morning
bathroom time within three minutes.

00:01:32.718 --> 00:01:35.470
Today was a close one.

00:01:35.470 --> 00:01:37.181
Oh, but I better hurry.

00:01:37.181 --> 00:01:40.851
Tomorrow's bathroom time will end up
being less than ten seconds as a penalty.

00:01:46.356 --> 00:01:49.109
What?!

00:01:49.109 --> 00:01:50.861
Nice, it looks good.

00:01:50.861 --> 00:01:52.905
Help!

00:01:52.905 --> 00:01:56.450
Code #3: Toilet paper (1-ply)

00:01:56.450 --> 00:01:59.328
must be replenished by the person
who used up the last roll.

00:01:59.328 --> 00:02:00.704
"Culprit"
must be replenished by the person
who used up the last roll.

00:02:01.455 --> 00:02:02.456
"Yesterday's leftovers"

00:02:02.456 --> 00:02:03.707
"Yesterday's leftovers"
"Donation"
All right, it's ready!

00:02:03.707 --> 00:02:04.041
"98 yen per pack"
All right, it's ready!

00:02:04.041 --> 00:02:04.958
"98 yen per pack"
Let's eat!

00:02:04.958 --> 00:02:06.043
"Bread crusts 30 yen"
"98 yen per pack"
Let's eat!

00:02:06.043 --> 00:02:07.794
Here you go, Ino-<i>sempai</i>.

00:02:07.794 --> 00:02:09.796
I made this sunny-side up egg for you!

00:02:09.796 --> 00:02:12.966
Wow, thank you very much, Hemo!

00:02:12.966 --> 00:02:13.842
Hey...

00:02:13.842 --> 00:02:15.010
Yes?

00:02:15.010 --> 00:02:17.804
Why do you always serve Ino last?

00:02:17.804 --> 00:02:20.432
Do you put in something special for her?

00:02:23.936 --> 00:02:25.604
It's love, of course!

00:02:25.604 --> 00:02:27.940
Thank you very much!

00:02:27.940 --> 00:02:29.274
What was that pause about?

00:02:29.274 --> 00:02:33.445
Code #4: Eat breakfast together in good spirits!

00:02:40.369 --> 00:02:42.871
Um... Roko...?

00:02:42.871 --> 00:02:45.958
Isn't it about time to use that thing?

00:02:45.958 --> 00:02:47.417
What thing?

00:02:47.417 --> 00:02:49.086
You know... That thing...

00:02:49.086 --> 00:02:50.546
"Roko's personal step"
You know... That thing...

00:02:50.546 --> 00:02:52.047
Never!

00:02:52.047 --> 00:02:56.593
Code #5: Morning washroom time
is ten minutes per two people!

00:02:56.593 --> 00:02:58.011
We've got an emergency.

00:02:58.011 --> 00:03:00.597
We don't have any strawberries
to wake Hayu with!

00:03:00.597 --> 00:03:03.267
Oh, then this should
do the trick, don't you think?

00:03:03.267 --> 00:03:04.601
It's red, too.

00:03:04.601 --> 00:03:06.144
Th-That's a bit...

00:03:06.144 --> 00:03:07.437
Let me try it!

00:03:09.398 --> 00:03:11.775
"Bread"
Hmph. It worked!

00:03:11.775 --> 00:03:14.778
"Bread"
Roko's bullying me!

00:03:14.778 --> 00:03:16.280
Not bad... it turns out.

00:03:16.280 --> 00:03:17.739
Ino?!

00:03:17.739 --> 00:03:20.909
Code #6: Idols must be punctual!

00:03:20.909 --> 00:03:22.828
Being on time is your own responsibility!

00:05:02.803 --> 00:05:04.096
"Could Be a Stalker?"

00:05:04.096 --> 00:05:06.974
"Could Be a Stalker?"
Could Be a Stalker?

00:05:06.974 --> 00:05:08.058
"Could Be a Stalker?"

00:05:08.225 --> 00:05:08.475
"Fruit Tart" "A Tart Feeling"

00:05:08.475 --> 00:05:10.269
"Fruit Tart" "A Tart Feeling"
Tada!

00:05:10.269 --> 00:05:14.231
How do you think this
amazing CD jacket turned out?!

00:05:15.357 --> 00:05:17.818
Incredible! It looks very professional!

00:05:17.818 --> 00:05:20.737
I didn't know what to expect
after the swimsuit shoot!

00:05:20.737 --> 00:05:23.156
But you've got some chops!

00:05:23.156 --> 00:05:26.493
Well of course, who do you think I am?

00:05:26.493 --> 00:05:31.707
And I'm selling those swimsuit shots
for 500 yen a piece...!

00:05:31.707 --> 00:05:32.875
What?!

00:05:32.875 --> 00:05:35.419
Now that we've finished the CD jacket,

00:05:35.419 --> 00:05:37.671
here's the next episode!

00:05:37.671 --> 00:05:39.840
Episode 6: Dropout Idol Fruit Tart.

00:05:39.840 --> 00:05:43.218
Come up with your autographs together!

00:05:43.218 --> 00:05:45.179
Our autographs?

00:05:45.179 --> 00:05:48.348
You girls are officially idols now.

00:05:48.348 --> 00:05:51.476
You should have established
your autographs by now.

00:05:51.476 --> 00:05:53.145
And you know...

00:05:53.145 --> 00:05:55.647
It could be worth a lot down the road...

00:05:55.647 --> 00:05:57.733
Why do you look away?

00:05:57.733 --> 00:05:59.067
Hmm...

00:05:59.067 --> 00:06:02.905
Come to think of it, I've never
thought of my autograph before.

00:06:02.905 --> 00:06:04.531
How about you, Ino-<i>sempai</i>?

00:06:04.531 --> 00:06:06.116
Wha--?! Me?!

00:06:06.116 --> 00:06:07.951
I-I...

00:06:11.914 --> 00:06:14.374
S-Something like this?

00:06:14.374 --> 00:06:17.377
Aw! It's really adorable!

00:06:17.377 --> 00:06:19.588
I've been thinking about it for a while now.

00:06:19.588 --> 00:06:22.549
Oh? But what is this
e-mail address-looking thing?

00:06:22.549 --> 00:06:24.343
Oh! That's...

00:06:24.343 --> 00:06:29.181
If there's a fan who's a girl, I'd like to be
friends with them so they could contact me.

00:06:29.181 --> 00:06:31.225
My goal is 100!

00:06:32.059 --> 00:06:33.936
Erase it right now.

00:06:33.936 --> 00:06:35.562
Contact saved!

00:06:35.562 --> 00:06:36.605
I got it!

00:06:36.605 --> 00:06:38.857
I thought of my autograph, too!

00:06:38.857 --> 00:06:39.983
Tada!

00:06:39.983 --> 00:06:42.611
What do you think?
It makes quite the impression, right?

00:06:42.611 --> 00:06:43.779
What?!

00:06:43.779 --> 00:06:47.658
These black wings and crosses
represent my inner darkness.

00:06:47.658 --> 00:06:51.662
And these powerful letters represent
my secret dark energy and its dark power!

00:06:51.662 --> 00:06:54.957
She'd probably regret this
in a few years so let's stop her.

00:06:54.957 --> 00:06:56.792
"Triggered the past"
I agree...

00:06:56.792 --> 00:06:57.584
"Triggered the past"

00:06:57.584 --> 00:06:58.001
"Hemo" "Nina Maehara"

00:06:58.001 --> 00:07:00.420
"Hemo" "Nina Maehara"
So, how about Nina and Hemo?

00:07:00.420 --> 00:07:02.631
"Hemo" "Nina Maehara"
Th-This is mine...

00:07:02.631 --> 00:07:04.716
"Hemo" "Nina Maehara"
What do you think of mine?

00:07:04.716 --> 00:07:06.134
"Hemo" "Nina Maehara"
Hmm...

00:07:06.134 --> 00:07:08.387
Nina, your letters are too small.

00:07:08.387 --> 00:07:10.430
Hemo, why do you have a <i>sakura </i>symbol in yours?

00:07:10.430 --> 00:07:12.224
Your last name is Midori, right?

00:07:12.224 --> 00:07:16.061
Oh? Don't you think those
two things suit each other?

00:07:16.061 --> 00:07:16.895
Huh?

00:07:16.895 --> 00:07:20.566
You know! Ino-<i>sempai</i>'s last name "Sakura"
and my last name "Midori"

00:07:20.566 --> 00:07:23.986
are both very nature-y and go well together!

00:07:23.986 --> 00:07:25.696
Right, Ino-<i>sempai</i>?

00:07:25.696 --> 00:07:28.031
Oh! You're right!

00:07:28.031 --> 00:07:32.077
Ino, it's about time you feel
a little scared for your safety now.

00:07:32.077 --> 00:07:36.290
But anyway, Nina, why are you always like this?

00:07:36.290 --> 00:07:38.041
What do you mean, "like this"?

00:07:38.041 --> 00:07:40.919
It's not just your writing,
you like buying small accessories

00:07:40.919 --> 00:07:44.173
and clothes that are too small for you
so you end up returning them.

00:07:45.132 --> 00:07:47.718
Why do you like small things so much?

00:07:47.718 --> 00:07:52.639
That means you only became
friends with me because I'm small...

00:07:52.639 --> 00:07:54.141
What?!

00:07:54.141 --> 00:07:56.059
I-Is that true...?

00:07:56.059 --> 00:08:00.230
Of course not! I'm kidding! I love you, Roko!

00:08:00.230 --> 00:08:02.983
N-No! You're mistaken!

00:08:02.983 --> 00:08:05.527
The reason I like small things

00:08:05.527 --> 00:08:08.238
is because I'm insecure
about the big parts of me.

00:08:08.238 --> 00:08:12.868
So I don't like you just because
you're small, Roko!

00:08:13.702 --> 00:08:17.539
R-Really?

00:08:17.539 --> 00:08:20.918
Of course! We're childhood friends, right?

00:08:20.918 --> 00:08:21.919
Nina!

00:08:21.919 --> 00:08:23.670
Roko!

00:08:23.670 --> 00:08:25.214
She's half-lying.

00:08:25.214 --> 00:08:26.673
I agree.

00:08:27.841 --> 00:08:30.552
All right! Injecting my rock spirit!

00:08:30.552 --> 00:08:32.846
Make it bigger and bigger!

00:08:34.556 --> 00:08:38.185
Oh yeah, Roko-<i>sempai</i>. Are you not
using your autograph from before?

00:08:38.185 --> 00:08:39.144
Huh?!

00:08:39.144 --> 00:08:39.394
"Let's Go Broko!"
Huh?!

00:08:39.394 --> 00:08:40.687
"Let's Go Broko!"
It was printed,

00:08:40.687 --> 00:08:43.941
"Let's Go Broko!"
but I used to have your autographed poster!

00:08:43.941 --> 00:08:46.443
It was my treasure!

00:08:46.443 --> 00:08:49.238
You're not using that autograph anymore?

00:08:49.238 --> 00:08:50.697
Never again.

00:08:50.697 --> 00:08:53.617
But it's really adorable!

00:08:53.617 --> 00:08:55.786
How would you know?

00:08:55.786 --> 00:08:58.830
You don't know what it's like to
have to keep using the autograph

00:08:58.830 --> 00:09:00.499
you made up when
you were six years old!

00:09:00.499 --> 00:09:01.416
"Roko Sekino."
you made up when
you were six years old!

00:09:01.416 --> 00:09:02.334
"Roko Sekino."

00:09:05.045 --> 00:09:06.213
Ino.

00:09:06.213 --> 00:09:07.256
Nina.

00:09:07.256 --> 00:09:08.340
Roko.

00:09:08.340 --> 00:09:09.424
Hemo.

00:09:09.424 --> 00:09:10.717
Hayu.

00:09:10.717 --> 00:09:16.640
Great! Everyone going based off
Ino's autograph turned out great!

00:09:16.640 --> 00:09:17.891
Now...

00:09:17.891 --> 00:09:20.394
You girls can sign thousands of autographs.

00:09:20.394 --> 00:09:21.228
What?

00:09:21.228 --> 00:09:23.856
Thousands?! What are you talking about?

00:09:23.856 --> 00:09:27.025
Oh? Didn't I mention this in the beginning?

00:09:27.025 --> 00:09:31.655
We're gonna have you girls sign your
autographs on every copy of the CD.

00:09:31.655 --> 00:09:34.533
You never did! We have to sign all of them?!

00:09:34.533 --> 00:09:39.997
Of course. Giving your all is
what you do as a newcomer idol.

00:09:39.997 --> 00:09:42.207
Anyway, relax.

00:09:42.207 --> 00:09:44.251
I mentioned "thousands" earlier,

00:09:44.251 --> 00:09:48.338
but with your current popularity,
the odds are worse than winning the lottery.

00:09:48.338 --> 00:09:49.840
Really?

00:09:49.840 --> 00:09:53.719
B-But, aren't idol's CDs really popular?

00:09:53.719 --> 00:09:56.221
Would you say your group is popular?

00:09:58.473 --> 00:10:00.142
I'm sorry...

00:10:00.142 --> 00:10:05.230
And plus, you girls made your debut
independently, not on a major label.

00:10:05.230 --> 00:10:08.192
We can't print that many copies to begin with.

00:10:08.192 --> 00:10:09.401
Independent?

00:10:09.401 --> 00:10:11.486
To put it simply...

00:10:11.486 --> 00:10:13.572
A major music label handles distribution
by paying for lots of ads!

00:10:13.572 --> 00:10:16.617
"Cream Anmitsu" "Riri's Win"
"Cream Anmitsu" "Collaboration Café"
A major music label handles distribution
by paying for lots of ads!

00:10:16.617 --> 00:10:20.120
Life is so easy that it's painful!

00:10:24.875 --> 00:10:27.002
What kind of mental picture is that?

00:10:28.128 --> 00:10:33.008
On the other hand, an independent label
has to do all those things on their own...

00:10:34.927 --> 00:10:37.513
You're over-exaggerating.

00:10:37.513 --> 00:10:41.683
To be direct, the greatest difference
is the financial muscle.

00:10:41.683 --> 00:10:43.727
Are there other things, too?

00:10:43.727 --> 00:10:45.062
You can say that.

00:10:45.062 --> 00:10:48.524
If this CD doesn't sell...

00:10:48.524 --> 00:10:50.567
If it doesn't sell...

00:10:50.567 --> 00:10:52.402
That means... death!

00:10:52.402 --> 00:10:53.654
Death?!

00:10:53.654 --> 00:10:57.199
We'll be in the greatest debt ever
and the group will have to break up!

00:10:57.199 --> 00:10:59.284
Everyone will be kicked out of Mouse House

00:10:59.284 --> 00:11:01.537
and be out in the cold!

00:11:01.537 --> 00:11:02.412
What?

00:11:02.412 --> 00:11:04.540
What?!

00:11:05.207 --> 00:11:07.292
I'm Hoho Kajino, Fruit Tart's manager.

00:11:07.292 --> 00:11:09.753
My birthday is August 8th and my blood type's O.

00:11:09.753 --> 00:11:12.005
I'm 165 cm and I weigh 51 kg.

00:11:12.005 --> 00:11:13.173
I love saké!

00:11:13.173 --> 00:11:15.050
What?! My age?!

00:11:21.056 --> 00:11:22.266
"Ino"

00:11:22.266 --> 00:11:24.518
"Ino"
<i>Dropout Idol Fruit Tart</i>!

00:11:24.518 --> 00:11:25.060
"Ino"

00:11:25.060 --> 00:11:27.312
"Fresh Vegetables"

00:11:27.813 --> 00:11:30.190
My name is Tone Honmachi.

00:11:30.190 --> 00:11:30.524
"Higashi-Koganei Okonomiyaki Tone"
My name is Tone Honmachi.

00:11:30.524 --> 00:11:34.945
"Higashi-Koganei Okonomiyaki Tone"
I'm the only daughter of this town's
favorite <i>okonomiyaki </i>joint.

00:11:34.945 --> 00:11:36.864
And...

00:11:36.864 --> 00:11:38.574
See you later!

00:11:38.574 --> 00:11:41.952
The newcomer idol, Fruit Tart's...

00:11:42.870 --> 00:11:45.163
...big, big, big fan!

00:11:45.163 --> 00:11:46.957
Did you study for the quiz?

00:11:46.957 --> 00:11:49.293
Yup, I'm pretty confident for this one!

00:11:50.669 --> 00:11:51.545
Huh?

00:11:51.545 --> 00:11:52.588
What was that?

00:11:52.588 --> 00:11:55.632
I thought I felt something strange just now...

00:11:55.632 --> 00:11:58.135
"Sai No Tsuno 2.0"
"Our Proud Curry"
"Slowly simmered rich flavor"

00:12:00.512 --> 00:12:02.389
"Koganei Academy"

00:12:02.389 --> 00:12:03.182
"Koganei Academy"
Hayu, how did the quiz go for you?

00:12:03.182 --> 00:12:05.267
Hayu, how did the quiz go for you?

00:12:05.267 --> 00:12:06.810
I think I did pretty good!

00:12:06.810 --> 00:12:10.063
English is one of my stronger subjects.

00:12:10.063 --> 00:12:12.441
I might get a failing grade...

00:12:12.441 --> 00:12:15.485
Oh... Then I can teach you!

00:12:15.485 --> 00:12:17.487
Really?

00:12:17.487 --> 00:12:18.447
I see.

00:12:18.447 --> 00:12:21.950
English is a weak subject for Miss Sakura.

00:12:21.950 --> 00:12:23.702
--I'm hungry.
--Same here.

00:12:23.702 --> 00:12:25.704
I wonder if there's anything
we can eat for ten yen.

00:12:25.704 --> 00:12:27.414
Oh, there's no such thing.

00:12:29.541 --> 00:12:33.003
We're set to make our CD debut!

00:12:33.003 --> 00:12:34.129
Congratulations!

00:12:34.129 --> 00:12:35.547
We'll be rooting for you girls.

00:12:35.547 --> 00:12:37.549
--Oh! They're so loved!
--I'm excited for this!

00:12:37.549 --> 00:12:39.092
--Oh! They're so loved!
--Thank you very much!

00:12:39.092 --> 00:12:40.219
"Metropolitan Koganei Park"

00:12:40.219 --> 00:12:41.094
"Metropolitan Koganei Park"
Wow, that's impressive.

00:12:41.094 --> 00:12:42.346
Wow, that's impressive.

00:12:42.346 --> 00:12:44.473
Thank you very much!

00:12:44.473 --> 00:12:46.058
This is for you!

00:12:47.226 --> 00:12:49.186
Good for you, Inocchi!

00:12:49.186 --> 00:12:52.105
They're the idols of Higako!

00:12:58.111 --> 00:13:00.489
Wh-Who the heck are you?!

00:13:00.489 --> 00:13:01.490
Who is she?

00:13:01.490 --> 00:13:04.034
What should I do? She's super sketchy!

00:13:04.034 --> 00:13:04.952
She's suspicious!

00:13:04.952 --> 00:13:06.495
Could she be a stalker?

00:13:06.495 --> 00:13:08.413
Ino-<i>sempai</i>'s in danger!

00:13:08.413 --> 00:13:12.125
--M-Miss Sakura is someone precious to me!
--Ino-<i>sempai </i>is someone precious to me!

00:13:14.044 --> 00:13:17.464
It's not looking good over there, Inocchi.

00:13:18.841 --> 00:13:22.219
What? A new member of Fruit Tart?

00:13:22.219 --> 00:13:23.428
Yes, I am.

00:13:23.428 --> 00:13:25.013
I'm Hemo Midori.

00:13:25.013 --> 00:13:27.224
I-I'm Tone Honmachi.

00:13:27.224 --> 00:13:29.685
I'm a classmate of Miss Sakura's.

00:13:31.186 --> 00:13:33.689
Hemo, Tone, you're both mistaken!

00:13:33.689 --> 00:13:36.275
Nobody's a suspicious person here!

00:13:36.275 --> 00:13:37.693
Ah, but...

00:13:37.693 --> 00:13:41.572
Why were you both following us?

00:13:42.614 --> 00:13:45.534
I-I was following a UFO...

00:13:45.534 --> 00:13:47.995
Really? Is it still around?

00:13:47.995 --> 00:13:51.790
Inocchi, they're both really suspicious.

00:13:51.790 --> 00:13:55.627
But I haven't heard any news about a new member.

00:13:55.627 --> 00:13:58.714
Well, the episode hasn't aired yet.

00:13:58.714 --> 00:14:01.091
It'll be revealed in this week's episode!

00:14:01.925 --> 00:14:04.887
Hemo was so moved by our performance,

00:14:04.887 --> 00:14:07.639
she transferred from
Cat Productions to work with us!

00:14:07.639 --> 00:14:09.391
I see.

00:14:09.391 --> 00:14:11.143
